# Physiological Development Taste Considerations & Philosophical Probes
#
# Somatic reverence, anti-reductionist biology, nutritional wisdom, and wonder probes in human health.

#>spw_cache_physio_taste
#:cache #!physio_dev
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Synthesize the aesthetic, somatic, and philosophical principles that elevate physiological care above reductionist biohacking and commercialized wellness."
  ~#resonance: "Cellular reverence, somatic attunement, biophilic harmony, and the sacred beauty of living human tissue"
}

^["the_body_as_sacred_symphony"]{
  critique: "The prevailing pathology of techno-modernity is viewing the human body as an obsolete, defective meat-machine to be aggressively hacked, optimized, and conquered."
  antidote: "Cultivating deep cellular reverence—recognizing that every heartbeat, breath, and enzymatic reaction is the result of four billion years of unbroken evolutionary wisdom."
  contrasts: #[
    "Obsessive wearable orthorexia vs. Somatic proprioception: Checking a watch to see if you slept well vs. waking up feeling rested in your bones",
    "Synthetic isolate mega-dosing vs. Whole living nourishment: Swallowing thirty synthetic chemical pills vs. sharing a bowl of mineral-rich wild fish stew",
    "Pathological age-denial vs. Vital graceful elderhood: Freezing faces with toxic paralytics vs. maintaining supple joints, clear mind, and vibrant presence"
  ]
}

^["the_illusion_of_the_isolated_biomarker"]{
  reductionist_trap: "Treating a single out-of-range lab biomarker as an isolated enemy to be crushed with an antagonist molecule, ignoring the systemic compensation network."
  holistic_insight: #[
    "Elevated cholesterol is often an acute phase response to vascular inflammation or endotoxemia, not a random liver defect",
    "High blood pressure is the body's desperate effort to push oxygenated blood through stiffened, calcified capillary beds",
    "Anxiety and depression are frequently neurochemical reflections of gut dysbiosis, systemic inflammation, or profound circadian disruption"
  ]
}

^["the_sacred_table_and_communal_feasting"]{
  cultural_truth: "Human beings do not simply ingest nutrients; we break bread together. The autonomic nervous system enters true parasympathetic rest only in the company of safe, loving others."
  practices: #[
    "Gratitude before meals: Pausing to acknowledge the life, soil, rain, and human labor that brought food to the table",
    "Unrushed mastication: Chewing food slowly and thoroughly, releasing salivary amylase and signaling stomach acid production",
    "Absence of digital screens: Keeping smartphones off the dining table to prevent cortisol spikes during nutrient absorption"
  ]
}

^"taste"{
  ~#taste: "True health is not the absence of symptoms, but the radiant, effortless overflow of biological energy into love, creativity, and service."
  ~#wonder: "Can a culture that has alienated itself from dirt, sun, darkness, and clean water ever truly heal its epidemic of chronic exhaustion without returning to the earth?"
}

^"invariants"{
  "Human physiology evolved to thrive on whole, minimally processed foods derived from living ecological systems.",
  "Biological optimization must never devolve into chronic anxiety, orthorexia, or somatic alienation.",
  "Physical health exists to serve human meaning, connection, and spiritual flourishing, not as an end in itself.",
}

#>wonder_physio_taste_1
?["Does eating whole-food meals in shared communal fellowship measurably improve postprandial glucose regulation compared to solitary eating of identical macronutrients?"]{
  #:depth #!biological ~#lens(psychoneuroendocrinology)
  ~#hypothesis: "Consuming an identical meal in a relaxed, warm social setting blunts peak postprandial blood glucose excursions by 20% compared to eating alone while staring at an email inbox, mediated by parasympathetic vagal stimulation."
  !probe{ "Conduct randomized crossover trial monitoring continuous glucose monitors (CGM) in adults consuming identical standard meals socially vs in solitary work environments." }
  $%[metabolism.cgm_postprandial_auc, autonomic.vagal_tone_hrv]
}

#>wonder_physio_taste_2
?["What is the minimum weekly threshold of unmediated contact with natural soil and biodiversity required to optimize the human immune microbiome?"]{
  #:depth #!biological ~#lens(environmental_immunology)
  ~#hypothesis: "Two hours weekly of bare-handed contact with biodiverse soil (gardening, native planting) increases skin and gut microbial diversity by 15% and significantly dampens atopic inflammatory markers."
  !probe{ "Conduct 12-week randomized trial of urban adults allocated to weekly organic soil gardening vs indoor exercise, tracking stool 16S rRNA sequencing and serum IgE." }
  $%[microbiome.shannon_diversity_index, immunology.total_serum_ige]
}
